WEBVTT

00:05.880 --> 00:07.330
Let me tell you a story about a slime.

00:07.330 --> 00:12.330
<b>Slime</b>

00:07.330 --> 00:12.330
<b>Lives near water</b>

00:08.130 --> 00:10.080
One day, the slime that Tia brought here

00:10.080 --> 00:12.330
to purify our waste water and
sewage started to multiply,

00:12.330 --> 00:15.960
and now there are lots of different types
of slimes that are all different colors here.

00:14.330 --> 00:16.290
<b>Normal</b>

00:14.330 --> 00:16.290
<b>Red</b>

00:14.340 --> 00:16.290
<b>Yellow</b>

00:14.340 --> 00:16.290
<b>Holy</b>

00:14.340 --> 00:16.290
<b>Green</b>

00:14.340 --> 00:16.290
<b>Black</b>

00:17.040 --> 00:19.040
They were all harmless,

00:19.040 --> 00:21.750
so I didn't really notice
that they'd been multiplying, but...

00:29.000 --> 00:31.170
Did it drink an entire barrel?

00:31.170 --> 00:32.880
A single slime drank it all?

00:32.880 --> 00:35.500
Even my dad can only drink
half a barrel at most.

00:35.500 --> 00:37.460
That alcohol was everyone's property!

00:37.460 --> 00:39.460
You can't go and drink it
without our permission!

00:39.460 --> 00:41.210
This deserves a severe punishment!

00:41.210 --> 00:42.170
That's right!

00:42.170 --> 00:43.040
Yeah!

00:43.040 --> 00:44.250
P-please wait a minute, everyone!

00:44.250 --> 00:46.040
Let's all calm down!

00:46.330 --> 00:49.500
This came as a big shock to
all the alcohol-loving residents here.

00:50.210 --> 00:52.750
And so began our village's first trial.

00:55.790 --> 00:56.960
<b>Guilty</b>

00:57.130 --> 00:58.630
Wait, um...
Let's burn it.<b></b>

00:58.630 --> 00:58.920
If we need fire, leave it to me!

00:58.920 --> 00:59.880
Guilty.
If we need fire, leave it to me!<b></b>

00:59.880 --> 01:00.790
But...
If we need fire, leave it to me!<b></b>

01:00.790 --> 01:03.290
What's going on?
Are we blowing something up?

01:03.290 --> 01:03.920
No, let's dry it out in the sun!

01:03.920 --> 01:05.630
No, let's dry it out in the sun!
Well, I feel bad for the poor thing,<b>
</b>so let's move away from the barbaric options...<b></b>

01:05.630 --> 01:07.790
Well, I feel bad for the poor thing,
so let's move away from the barbaric options...

01:07.790 --> 01:09.630
How about we go with a
short confinement as a punishment?

01:07.790 --> 01:10.960
<b>Confinement</b>

01:09.630 --> 01:11.920
But that was our precious alcohol!

01:13.290 --> 01:15.540
Jeez, this kind of stuff happens
because you're too soft!

01:15.540 --> 01:18.290
Um, everyone?
We're talking about a slime here.

01:18.920 --> 01:22.880
Even if we punish it, I'm not sure
that it's going to reflect on its actions.

01:23.290 --> 01:25.250
Well, you have a point.

01:25.540 --> 01:27.170
It is a slime, after all.

01:27.170 --> 01:29.170
And so, that slime was acquitted.
I got a little too fired up back there...<b></b>

01:29.170 --> 01:29.750
And so, that slime was acquitted.

01:30.170 --> 01:35.880
After that, it began to pop up during our feasts
and celebrations so that it could join us.

01:36.880 --> 01:40.380
Oh well. I think it's alright
if we have one slime like that.

01:40.380 --> 01:42.250
Too many would be a problem, though.

01:52.750 --> 01:54.750
<b>Farming Life in Another World</b>

01:54.170 --> 02:01.750
When you open your eyes and see
that pure white light, the story begins

02:01.750 --> 02:08.460
Stepping forth into a new world,
what kind of flowers will we make bloom?

02:08.670 --> 02:16.040
Even if it's cloudy,
even if we get dirty from a puddle

02:16.040 --> 02:18.880
We continue on

02:18.880 --> 02:25.630
There's a future we can't imagine
waiting for us, I'm sure of it

02:25.960 --> 02:29.540
Meeting, meeting, and connecting

02:29.540 --> 02:32.830
If you smile,
everyone around you will smile too

02:32.830 --> 02:36.880
Let's plant a small seed and nurture it

02:36.880 --> 02:40.960
One day it'll become a large flower

02:40.960 --> 02:44.460
Turn regrets and failures into fuel

02:44.460 --> 02:47.750
So that you're overflowing with colorful happiness

02:47.750 --> 02:51.960
We'll join hands and share

02:51.960 --> 02:57.790
Spread across the world, Flower Ring

03:17.130 --> 03:18.460
The season is autumn.

03:19.040 --> 03:21.960
The summers here aren't
particularly hot or anything,

03:21.960 --> 03:26.380
but it's still nice when things cool down a bit
and we can get some more work done.

03:26.380 --> 03:27.460
And here's the result.

03:29.210 --> 03:30.580
This is making me hungry.

03:30.580 --> 03:31.920
Autumn means eating!

03:36.960 --> 03:39.250
Hey, stop taking all the meat.

03:39.250 --> 03:41.210
I'm eating vegetables, too!

03:42.670 --> 03:43.710
It's delicious!

03:44.170 --> 03:47.580
These are all new types of mushrooms
that we didn't have in Howling Village.

03:48.080 --> 03:51.040
Man, I really love hot pots.

03:51.250 --> 03:54.750
If we could get seafood here,
these would taste even better.

03:57.250 --> 04:00.880
What exactly are you referring to
when you say seafood?

04:00.880 --> 04:02.250
Let's see...

04:02.500 --> 04:05.040
<b>Cod</b>

04:02.750 --> 04:05.210
Stuff like cod or crabs or monkfish.

04:03.000 --> 04:05.040
<b>Crab</b>

04:03.500 --> 04:05.040
<b>Monkfish</b>

04:05.210 --> 04:07.290
We can make broth from kombu!

04:05.250 --> 04:07.290
<b>Kombu</b>

04:07.290 --> 04:09.630
Then we could make a chanco hotpot with miso!

04:10.500 --> 04:12.290
Start researching those things immediately!

04:12.290 --> 04:13.630
I've found information on them!

04:13.630 --> 04:17.130
What do I do?
I've never even seen the ocean.

04:17.130 --> 04:18.540
Did you say crabs?

04:18.630 --> 04:20.380
Can you eat those?

04:18.630 --> 04:22.080
<b>Speaking from experience</b>

04:20.380 --> 04:22.080
They're really hard!

04:22.250 --> 04:23.380
Kombu...

04:23.380 --> 04:25.540
It sounds like something terrifying.

04:25.670 --> 04:26.580
<b>The Raging Storm</b>

04:25.670 --> 04:26.580
<b>Kombu</b>

04:26.790 --> 04:27.830
Broth?

04:27.830 --> 04:30.710
That's the soup-like thing you showed me
how to prepare earlier, right?

04:30.710 --> 04:31.670
That's right.

04:31.670 --> 04:33.580
Is chanco a kind of fish, too?

04:32.420 --> 04:34.880
<b>The Deep Sea Sage</b>

04:32.420 --> 04:34.880
<b>Chanco</b>

04:34.250 --> 04:35.670
If we need ocean access,

04:35.670 --> 04:37.920
there's a port city within the boundaries
of the Demonic Kingdom.

04:38.630 --> 04:41.960
You can reach it if you
head south from this village.

04:41.960 --> 04:44.420
They do a lot of trading of ocean products,

04:44.420 --> 04:47.040
so we might be able to find those fish there.

04:47.040 --> 04:49.330
Okay then, I'll fly over and check it out.

04:49.330 --> 04:51.250
I'll accompany you.

04:51.250 --> 04:53.420
We can ask a merchant I know for help.

04:53.420 --> 04:55.000
Let's get started right away!

04:55.000 --> 04:57.130
I'll take care of the miso!

04:58.790 --> 05:01.000
They all really like hotpots, huh?

05:01.880 --> 05:03.080
Indeed.

05:03.540 --> 05:05.330
See you later.

05:05.330 --> 05:07.330
We're counting on you.

05:07.330 --> 05:10.130
When it comes to food, everyone here
gets very motivated to work.

05:10.790 --> 05:15.500
Well, nothing makes me happier as a farmer
than seeing them happily enjoying my food.

05:18.580 --> 05:21.750
And so, the return of the group
that set out in earnest took place...

05:21.830 --> 05:23.830
<b>3 days later</b>

05:22.580 --> 05:23.630
3 days later.

05:23.830 --> 05:31.290
<b>Goroun Company President</b>

05:23.830 --> 05:31.290
<b>Michael Goroun</b>

05:24.080 --> 05:25.960
My name is Michael.

05:25.960 --> 05:31.290
I'm a merchant from the city of Shashato
in the Demonic Kingdom.

05:31.460 --> 05:33.000
I'm the mayor, Hiraku.

05:33.420 --> 05:35.830
Thank you for coming
all the way here to our village.

05:35.830 --> 05:37.080
It's nothing.

05:37.080 --> 05:40.130
This is part of my job as a merchant.

05:41.500 --> 05:44.290
These are the marine products
I brought from the city of Shashato.

05:44.290 --> 05:46.210
They are our pride and joy.

05:46.540 --> 05:49.210
With regards to the seaweed
called kombu that you requested,

05:49.210 --> 05:50.960
our fishermen normally throw it
back into the ocean

05:50.960 --> 05:52.960
even if they pull some up in their nets.

05:52.960 --> 05:54.500
Huh? So...

05:54.630 --> 05:56.000
No need to worry.

05:56.000 --> 05:59.460
I'll have my men collect some right away.

05:59.630 --> 06:02.630
We'll have it dried and ready before long.

06:02.630 --> 06:03.920
I see.

06:04.170 --> 06:09.710
With regards to my visit here today,
I have three main goals.

06:10.420 --> 06:13.630
The first is to properly greet you

06:13.630 --> 06:16.750
and thank you for requesting
to do business with us.

06:17.210 --> 06:21.630
The second is to suggest more opportunities
for us to trade goods and do business.

06:22.330 --> 06:24.380
And my third goal, if possible,

06:24.380 --> 06:29.630
is to become the official government
purveyor for this village.

06:29.630 --> 06:31.250
Official government purveyor?

06:31.250 --> 06:35.130
It means he wants to handle all trade
between us and the outside world.

06:35.130 --> 06:37.670
You're being quite direct
in what you're asking us for.

06:37.670 --> 06:42.630
I'm always careful to not be so indirect
that my intentions are misinterpreted.

06:43.080 --> 06:46.670
All of the crops you have here
are very enticing.

06:47.130 --> 06:49.670
If you allow me the opportunity,

06:49.670 --> 06:53.630
I can get you several times more value
when trading them.

06:55.790 --> 06:59.830
There are a lot of people who want
to do trade with this village.

07:00.170 --> 07:02.630
As I said, if possible.

07:03.040 --> 07:06.210
I'd like to ask that you first
have a look at a list of the products

07:06.210 --> 07:09.080
that my company handles the trading of.

07:09.080 --> 07:11.500
And from there,
we can discuss my proposition.

07:14.460 --> 07:17.960
We were able to cover a lot of
important ground with today's talks.

07:17.960 --> 07:21.710
Next time, I'd like it if we were able to
discuss the alcohol produced in this village...

07:21.710 --> 07:23.670
You can't have the alcohol!

07:26.040 --> 07:27.630
Pardon me.

07:27.630 --> 07:29.710
I'll leave things here for today.

07:31.330 --> 07:35.250
Well, he seemed like
a skilled merchant, didn't he?

07:35.250 --> 07:36.580
Yeah.

07:36.580 --> 07:38.790
It'll be a big help having him
handle our negotiations.

07:38.790 --> 07:41.000
And even though he's handling things for us,

07:41.000 --> 07:42.960
we'll end up getting more goods
when we trade now!

07:43.250 --> 07:46.210
It really didn't seem like he had
any intention of trying to deceive us.

07:46.210 --> 07:50.080
Yeah. I hope our relationship with him
goes smoothly from here on out.

07:50.920 --> 07:54.210
It seemed like he was
really frightened there at the end...

07:54.210 --> 07:55.380
but oh well.

07:55.380 --> 07:58.630
That's to be expected
when you're talking to a dragon.

08:04.040 --> 08:06.130
The Great Tree Village, huh?

08:13.880 --> 08:15.960
That was scary!

08:16.170 --> 08:18.580
<b>3 days earlier</b>

08:21.880 --> 08:24.830
<b>Shashato City</b>

08:23.380 --> 08:24.830
A visitor?

08:25.000 --> 08:26.710
Without an appointment?

08:26.710 --> 08:27.500
Yes.

08:27.500 --> 08:29.460
They'd like to talk business with you.

08:29.460 --> 08:32.130
I couldn't be any busier now.

08:32.460 --> 08:35.000
My name is Michael Goroun.

08:35.000 --> 08:38.880
I work as the head of the largest
trading company in this city.

08:39.500 --> 08:42.170
If it's nothing major,
can't you guys handle it?

08:42.170 --> 08:45.130
Why do they need to see me specifically?

08:45.130 --> 08:48.790
They requested you by name
when they arrived.

08:48.790 --> 08:51.170
They've even brought goods from their farm.

08:51.170 --> 08:52.830
I wasn't sure what to do.

08:52.830 --> 08:56.080
They already brought goods with them?
Don't they know the rules?

08:56.080 --> 08:59.670
If you guys can't handle it on your own,
then just refer them somewhere el-

09:01.920 --> 09:03.630
No, I'll meet with them.

09:03.630 --> 09:05.580
Huh? Okay.

09:06.500 --> 09:09.670
My merchant's intuition is telling me
that I can't ignore this.

09:09.670 --> 09:13.420
This strange feeling
welling up inside of me is...

09:14.420 --> 09:17.420
I'm so glad that you remember me.

09:17.420 --> 09:19.290
Of course.

09:19.290 --> 09:20.790
If I remember correctly,

09:20.790 --> 09:24.080
the last time we had the pleasure of meeting
was at your birthday party.

09:24.250 --> 09:27.210
I can't believe the young lady of
the Chrome family is here.

09:27.500 --> 09:30.580
My head would have rolled
if I'd have sent her away.

09:32.830 --> 09:34.580
And who have you brought with you?

09:34.580 --> 09:36.580
Oh, she's...

09:36.580 --> 09:39.330
I'm Lastismoon of the dragons.

09:39.330 --> 09:41.210
Please call me Lasty.

09:41.380 --> 09:42.830
Lastismoon?!

09:43.580 --> 09:46.080
Could she really be that crazy dragon?

09:44.130 --> 09:46.540
<b>Crazy Dragon Lastismoon</b>

09:46.710 --> 09:48.250
She's just a child!

09:49.330 --> 09:52.250
The daughter of one of the most powerful
families of the Demonic Kingdom

09:52.250 --> 09:54.130
and a dangerous dragon.

09:54.130 --> 09:57.170
The risks of trading with them are too high.

09:54.830 --> 09:57.460
<b>Risk</b>

09:57.580 --> 10:00.580
So what brings you here today?

10:00.790 --> 10:02.920
But I can't just ignore them!

10:04.290 --> 10:06.880
We'd like you to purchase these from us.

10:08.080 --> 10:10.920
And in exchange for them,
there are some things we'd like you to find.

10:12.960 --> 10:14.830
What's going on here?

10:14.830 --> 10:18.500
I'm being stared down by a dragon
while being surrounded by lizardmen.

10:18.920 --> 10:22.630
I'm about to enter
some outrageous trade talks.

10:22.630 --> 10:27.130
Was that feeling I had before
a warning of impending danger?

10:30.130 --> 10:31.380
These are...

10:31.380 --> 10:33.250
those fruit that have entered
the Demonic Kingdom

10:33.250 --> 10:34.630
that people have been talking about!

10:34.630 --> 10:37.210
Each one of these
can fetch several silver coins.

10:37.500 --> 10:39.500
And look how many they've brought!

10:40.130 --> 10:41.830
<b>Risk</b>

10:41.960 --> 10:44.880
The goods you wanted
were from the ocean, correct?

10:44.880 --> 10:46.130
That's right!

10:46.750 --> 10:49.210
This port is my territory.

10:49.210 --> 10:51.830
I can find you whatever you need.

10:52.710 --> 10:53.920
Because that's...

10:53.920 --> 10:56.460
the job of a merchant!

10:56.920 --> 10:59.750
I can't let this chance get away!

11:00.000 --> 11:03.130
Hey you. Go to the port and bring me
their best catches from this morning.

11:03.130 --> 11:04.040
Okay!

11:04.040 --> 11:06.210
And after that begin preparing
for me to travel.

11:06.210 --> 11:07.420
Uh, okay!

11:07.420 --> 11:10.000
I'll take part in the delivery myself.

11:10.000 --> 11:12.000
Are the goods going to the capital?

11:12.000 --> 11:15.290
No, they're going to The Great Tree Village
in The Forest of Death.

11:15.290 --> 11:18.290
I'll carry the stuff,
so I can give you a ride too.

11:18.540 --> 11:20.080
Forest of Death?

11:18.540 --> 11:21.380
<b>Unease</b>

11:18.540 --> 11:21.380
<b>Risk</b>

11:20.080 --> 11:21.380
Give me a ride?

11:28.380 --> 11:30.380
He's a merchant from Shashato.

11:32.750 --> 11:35.210
Oh, the merchant came with you?

11:35.210 --> 11:35.790
<b>Illegal Demon Spider</b>

11:35.210 --> 11:35.790
<b>Killer Angels</b>

11:35.210 --> 11:37.170
<b>Angel of Annihilation</b>

11:35.210 --> 11:37.170
<b>Inferno Wolf</b>

11:38.380 --> 11:40.380
The mayor seems normal.

11:41.000 --> 11:43.040
<b>Vampire Princess</b>

11:43.170 --> 11:44.830
You can't have the alcohol!

11:54.040 --> 11:55.790
I-I survived it...

11:55.790 --> 11:58.380
I managed to finish my business
with that terrifying group

11:58.380 --> 12:00.580
while having a smile on my face.

12:00.960 --> 12:03.500
That was the best deal of my life.

12:03.500 --> 12:06.920
Huge profits are waiting for me
from here on out.

12:07.750 --> 12:09.080
However...

12:12.380 --> 12:15.130
I'm not sure if my body can handle this.

12:24.080 --> 12:25.830
Here it is, real seafood!

12:26.580 --> 12:29.170
Maybe next time I'll ask him
for shrimp or squid.

12:39.670 --> 12:42.710
This is the third time a dragon
has attacked this village.

12:42.880 --> 12:44.500
I think.

12:44.500 --> 12:47.130
Is this one related to Dryme again?

12:47.460 --> 12:52.000
For the record, the three angel squad
in charge of patrolling the skies

12:52.000 --> 12:54.330
was quickly able to spot this dragon.

12:55.960 --> 12:58.500
However stopping a dragon
proved to be difficult.

12:59.000 --> 13:01.250
But seriously, what is that dragon doing?

13:01.250 --> 13:02.380
Acting smug?

13:07.790 --> 13:09.630
Okay, so you're challenging me.

13:09.630 --> 13:11.250
You want a fight, right?

13:11.250 --> 13:12.460
In that case...

13:16.710 --> 13:17.920
I missed?!

13:18.420 --> 13:20.420
...is what I want them to think.

13:20.420 --> 13:21.670
Once more!

13:22.500 --> 13:23.630
Defeated.

13:29.630 --> 13:31.420
Ouch...

13:31.420 --> 13:33.920
Aw, you got me.

13:34.080 --> 13:35.420
I surrender!

13:35.420 --> 13:36.830
Just kidding!

13:37.130 --> 13:38.920
Why did you do that?

13:38.920 --> 13:42.290
Well you see,
it really isn't that big of an issue.

13:42.290 --> 13:44.040
But you burned the forest?

13:44.040 --> 13:46.080
Okay then, just give me a minute
and I'll come up with

13:46.080 --> 13:48.130
a super important reason why I did that.

13:49.290 --> 13:50.670
Hey!

13:50.670 --> 13:52.670
Wait a minute, mayor!

13:55.080 --> 13:56.750
I'm sorry, she's...

13:57.670 --> 13:59.250
It's little Drymey!

13:59.250 --> 14:00.170
Little?

14:00.170 --> 14:06.630
<b>Explaining</b>

14:00.580 --> 14:03.880
According to Dryme's explanation,
her name is Hakuren.

14:03.880 --> 14:06.380
She's his older sister.

14:06.830 --> 14:08.920
This is your fault, you know.

14:08.920 --> 14:12.170
You said you were giving away
Lasty as a bride.

14:12.170 --> 14:13.130
Bride?

14:13.130 --> 14:14.330
No, I...

14:14.330 --> 14:15.710
You totally said it!

14:15.710 --> 14:19.250
You said you wanted to marry her off
to the mayor of this village someday!

14:19.250 --> 14:20.080
Dryme?

14:20.080 --> 14:21.460
It's not like that!

14:21.460 --> 14:22.500
I might have said something kind of like that
while I was drinking, but...

14:22.500 --> 14:24.830
I'll do it one day for the prosperity of our tribe!
I might have said something kind of like that<b>
</b>while I was drinking, but...<b></b>

14:24.830 --> 14:27.000
I'll do it one day for the prosperity of our tribe!
As the person in question,<b>
</b>it makes it really hard to comment on this.<b></b>

14:27.000 --> 14:27.830
As the person in question,
it makes it really hard to comment on this.

14:28.080 --> 14:30.080
So that's why I came out here

14:30.080 --> 14:32.460
to see what kind of person
he was marrying her off to.

14:32.460 --> 14:34.960
Then why couldn't you just
come visit normally?

14:34.960 --> 14:38.130
Everyone always talks about
how strong the mayor here is,

14:38.130 --> 14:40.630
so I wanted to come play with you a little.

14:41.130 --> 14:43.170
It's not just that.

14:43.380 --> 14:45.210
She's mostly here to vent anger.

14:45.210 --> 14:47.210
Of course I am!

14:47.210 --> 14:49.330
Do you think I could just let it slide

14:49.330 --> 14:51.420
that my little niece is going to find
a husband before I do?!

14:51.420 --> 14:54.420
I mean come on,
she's 900 years younger than me!

14:53.710 --> 14:55.420
<b>900 Years Older</b>

14:53.710 --> 14:55.420
<b>900 Years Younger</b>

14:54.420 --> 14:56.960
I can't accept this!

14:56.960 --> 14:58.670
It's ridiculous!

14:58.880 --> 15:00.250
Don't you agre-

15:00.250 --> 15:02.040
It's fine if you want to come play,

15:02.040 --> 15:04.880
but you shouldn't be causing
problems for people.

15:05.250 --> 15:06.170
And it goes without saying, that you're
going to clean up this mess, right?

15:06.170 --> 15:09.000
Okay, I get it!
And it goes without saying, that you're<b>
</b>going to clean up this mess, right?<b></b>

15:09.000 --> 15:11.460
<b>Clean Up</b>

15:12.750 --> 15:15.670
So you two are always eating food
that tastes this good?

15:15.670 --> 15:18.750
Well, I'm not always
imposing on everyone here.

15:18.750 --> 15:20.710
Only about three out of every ten days.

15:20.710 --> 15:22.330
Wow, lucky!

15:22.330 --> 15:22.750
Maybe it's five days...

15:22.750 --> 15:24.130
She's already fitting in...
Maybe it's five days...<b></b>

15:24.130 --> 15:24.790
She's already fitting in...
Five days?!<b></b>

15:24.790 --> 15:25.250
Five days?!

15:25.250 --> 15:26.420
Mayor.

15:26.630 --> 15:28.830
I'm sorry that my aunt is-

15:28.830 --> 15:30.420
Hey, Lasty?

15:30.420 --> 15:33.500
...that Big Sis Hakuren
is causing so much trouble.

15:33.500 --> 15:35.750
It's nothing you need to
apologize about, Lasty.

15:36.290 --> 15:40.460
Oh right, I heard you have some
really fun games here.

15:40.460 --> 15:43.040
Like the one where you line up
the little square things.

15:43.040 --> 15:44.630
You mean mahjong?

15:44.630 --> 15:46.250
I want to try that.

15:46.250 --> 15:48.040
You play with four people, right?

15:48.040 --> 15:50.460
Hey mayor, let's play!

15:50.460 --> 15:52.670
I don't want to leave here
only having lost to you!

15:52.670 --> 15:54.460
Fine by me.

15:55.080 --> 15:57.250
So, first let me explain the rules.

15:57.250 --> 15:58.540
I'll be fine!

15:58.540 --> 15:59.670
I can figure it out!

15:59.670 --> 16:00.790
Really?

16:01.210 --> 16:03.210
But more importantly...

16:03.540 --> 16:05.290
what should we bet?

16:07.250 --> 16:08.670
I see.

16:08.670 --> 16:12.540
This way it's more fun
than just playing the game.

16:12.540 --> 16:14.670
I think we should take it easy at first...

16:14.670 --> 16:15.750
Mayor.

16:15.750 --> 16:19.080
What would you normally bet
when playing mahjong like this?

16:19.420 --> 16:24.040
Even if you want me to bet something,
I don't really have anything I can bet.

16:24.540 --> 16:26.380
So then should we have
a punishment for the loser?

16:26.380 --> 16:29.460
The only thing I can think to do
is play strip mahjong.

16:30.170 --> 16:31.380
That sounds great!

16:31.380 --> 16:33.960
So the loser gets a taste of humiliation.

16:34.080 --> 16:36.880
No, no, I don't want to force anyone
to do anything they don't want to!

16:36.880 --> 16:38.330
Right, Lasty?

16:38.330 --> 16:40.920
If we're competing,
then there's no way I can lose...

16:40.920 --> 16:41.960
Excuse me, Lasty?

16:41.960 --> 16:44.170
...as a member of the dragon clan!

16:44.630 --> 16:47.710
I have a feeling that
things are going to get bad.

16:51.540 --> 16:53.210
Ah, that's chii!

16:53.710 --> 16:54.830
That's riichi!

16:54.830 --> 16:56.960
Too bad... ron!

16:56.960 --> 16:58.210
What?!

16:58.500 --> 17:01.500
This is my fault for carelessly
suggesting this idea.

17:03.420 --> 17:05.750
This is indeed shameful.

17:06.040 --> 17:08.500
The dragons are all very competitive,

17:08.500 --> 17:10.750
Aw, I was so close.
and they can't stand losing.<b></b>

17:10.750 --> 17:13.460
Let's keep going!
This led to a very serious game<b>
</b>of strip mahjong starting.<b></b>

17:13.880 --> 17:15.580
You're new to this, aren't you?

17:15.580 --> 17:17.040
And you're wearing the least clothing.

17:17.040 --> 17:18.630
How are you so confident?!

17:18.960 --> 17:21.880
Now that it's come to this,
I wanted to carefully rack up some points

17:21.880 --> 17:24.580
and end things while maintaining
the peace, but...

17:26.000 --> 17:27.380
something isn't right.

17:27.830 --> 17:29.330
Seriously, what's happening here?

17:29.330 --> 17:30.880
How am I losing?!

17:30.880 --> 17:32.670
I'm on my last piece of clothing!

17:32.880 --> 17:35.670
Don't tell me they're using
some kind of magic trickery?!

17:36.670 --> 17:38.500
Are they using telekinesis to rewrite the tiles?!

17:38.880 --> 17:40.790
Can they see through the back of my tiles?!

17:41.250 --> 17:42.210
No.

17:42.460 --> 17:44.420
There isn't anything written on this one.

17:44.420 --> 17:45.420
Is it an extra?

17:45.420 --> 17:47.040
I'm overthinking it.
Some tiles are just like that.<b></b>

17:47.630 --> 17:49.040
In any case,

17:50.540 --> 17:52.880
my chance has finally arrived.

17:52.880 --> 17:54.790
I can score a double yakuman.

17:55.250 --> 17:58.080
I can end the whole thing
with a single move.

17:58.380 --> 17:59.500
But...

17:59.710 --> 18:03.880
<b>Sad Memories</b>

18:00.500 --> 18:02.540
of course it had to be this tile again!

18:03.540 --> 18:04.750
It doesn't matter.

18:04.750 --> 18:07.960
I'll never beat the dragons
if I'm paralyzed by fear!

18:09.210 --> 18:10.210
Ron!

18:10.670 --> 18:12.790
That's about right.

18:13.330 --> 18:15.130
Okay, pants off!

18:15.130 --> 18:18.080
Pants off! Pants off! Pants off!

18:18.210 --> 18:20.920
Pants off! Pants off! Pants off!

18:21.170 --> 18:22.170
I am defeated!

18:24.330 --> 18:27.460
The dragons are gathering
in that village again?

18:27.460 --> 18:32.080
Yes. The ancient dragon Hakuren
was spotted as well.

18:32.080 --> 18:35.960
No way... They're got enough power
to conquer a whole country now.

18:36.290 --> 18:38.500
Can we afford to simply sit back and watch?

18:39.710 --> 18:41.540
More importantly, Beezel...

18:41.830 --> 18:44.420
Yes. Do you have an idea?

18:44.830 --> 18:45.920
No.

18:44.830 --> 18:52.540
<b>Demon Lord Galgardo</b>

18:45.920 --> 18:48.580
It's my daughter.
She's been in a bad mood lately.

18:48.580 --> 18:52.540
She hasn't said anything to me all day
besides good morning.

18:52.710 --> 18:54.290
Is this her rebellious phase?

18:54.290 --> 18:58.330
So anyways... we need to focus on
preparing our military forces immediately!

18:58.330 --> 19:00.170
We'll need to secure the funds we need-

19:00.170 --> 19:00.460
I resign. Signed Randan.

19:00.330 --> 19:03.790
<b>Letter of Resignation</b>

19:00.460 --> 19:01.290
Randan?!
I resign. Signed Randan.<b></b>

19:01.290 --> 19:01.920
I resign. Signed Randan.

19:01.920 --> 19:03.790
Ah, he ran away.

19:03.920 --> 19:06.670
Is this a joke?!

19:07.170 --> 19:10.880
So if you divide these apples
between three people,

19:10.880 --> 19:13.630
how many apples will you have to eat?

19:13.960 --> 19:16.460
I really wish I could just them all, though!

19:18.380 --> 19:20.670
She's really come into her own here.

19:21.210 --> 19:23.630
After attacking The Great Tree Village,

19:23.630 --> 19:26.330
Hakuren decided to stay here
for the time being.

19:23.630 --> 19:26.330
<b>My Room</b>

19:23.630 --> 19:26.330
<b>Signed by Hakuren</b>

19:26.540 --> 19:27.500
Surprisingly, she's very skilled
and able to handle any job here.

19:27.500 --> 19:29.630
There we go. Nice and easy.
Surprisingly, she's very skilled<b>
</b>and able to handle any job here.<b></b>

19:29.630 --> 19:30.380
There we go. Nice and easy.

19:30.380 --> 19:33.080
<b>The Great Tree Village by Hakuren</b>

19:30.540 --> 19:33.080
But she complains about
anything she's asked to do.

19:33.250 --> 19:35.380
Every time I turn around,
she's in her room doing nothing.

19:35.380 --> 19:36.880
I don't wanna to it.

19:36.880 --> 19:39.420
Why do you complain so much?

19:39.420 --> 19:43.630
I'm hoping that one day maybe people
will stop asking me to do things.

19:44.130 --> 19:46.130
I had no choice but to order her to start
digging holes and then filling them back in.

19:46.130 --> 19:48.460
Okay, enough! I give up!
I had no choice but to order her to start<b>
</b>digging holes and then filling them back in.<b></b>

19:48.460 --> 19:49.960
Okay, enough! I give up!
She gave up on day one.<b></b>

19:50.330 --> 19:53.420
In the end we settled on her teaching
reading, writing, and math.

19:53.420 --> 19:55.330
She became the village teacher.

19:55.330 --> 19:58.290
And that's why learning to
read, write, and do math,

19:58.290 --> 20:01.040
will help you all a lot
in your day to day lives!

20:01.290 --> 20:03.170
Listen up, I want all of you
to work really hard,

20:03.170 --> 20:06.420
so that one day I don't have to
work anymore, okay?

20:06.420 --> 20:07.790
Okay!

20:07.790 --> 20:10.130
I think her motivation
might not be the greatest.

20:13.210 --> 20:16.670
Please, we beg of you to spare our lives.

20:17.830 --> 20:19.540
What are you talking about?

20:20.130 --> 20:23.420
According to the lamia girls...

20:23.420 --> 20:25.540
at some point, the younger animals

20:25.540 --> 20:28.710
decided to clear a dungeon they found
in the middle of the forest..

20:28.710 --> 20:32.580
And then the lamia were forced to
quickly flee their homes.

20:34.710 --> 20:38.670
<b>Praise me</b>

20:35.420 --> 20:37.000
They didn't know what they were doing,

20:37.000 --> 20:38.670
but they still caused the girls
a lot of trouble.

20:39.000 --> 20:40.500
What should we do?

20:40.920 --> 20:45.040
They came all the way here
to seek our aid and protection.

20:45.040 --> 20:47.210
I don't think it would be proper
to turn them away.

20:47.710 --> 20:51.210
In the end, we decided to trade
the precious gems the lamia mined

20:51.210 --> 20:53.630
for some of our crops.

20:53.630 --> 20:56.880
After that, they went back to
their original homes.

20:57.210 --> 21:00.080
I'd appreciate it if we could
keep trading from now on.

21:00.080 --> 21:02.540
Of course!
Just ask us for whatever you want!

21:02.540 --> 21:05.920
They're so genuinely excited about this
that it's making me awkward.

21:06.290 --> 21:08.920
Okay then, I have something
I'd like to request.

21:08.920 --> 21:09.670
Yes?

21:09.670 --> 21:12.540
It's fine if it's only when
you're visiting here,

21:12.540 --> 21:14.750
but I'd appreciate it if you could
put some clothes on.

21:16.460 --> 21:21.380
That might be part of their culture,
but I really had trouble not staring.

21:22.500 --> 21:25.630
After that, the lamia formed
the Lamia Delivery Service

21:25.630 --> 21:28.380
and started carrying
our trading goods for us.

21:29.040 --> 21:32.540
With everything said and done,
I'm glad we found some reliable neighbors.

21:33.000 --> 21:35.790
Between this and the increased trade
with other cities and areas,

21:35.790 --> 21:38.420
it really feels like the village
has reached a new level.

21:38.880 --> 21:41.080
Since we've increased
the amount of trade we're doing,

21:41.080 --> 21:42.460
how about we plant more crops?

21:42.460 --> 21:43.500
Yeah.

21:53.290 --> 21:55.880
It appears that village is indeed
amassing military might

21:55.880 --> 21:58.290
and planning something foul!

21:58.290 --> 22:00.250
They may be convincing
Flowrem to stay there

22:00.250 --> 22:03.460
so that they can use her as
a hostage if they need to!

22:03.460 --> 22:07.460
We should begin gathering
our troops at once, Princess!

22:08.790 --> 22:10.170
I understand.

22:10.880 --> 22:15.000
We must defeat that village
and save Flowrem.

22:30.170 --> 22:38.920
I can feel the soft seasonal winds,
gently on my fingertips

22:39.250 --> 22:47.830
Let's search for what we love
in the clouds floating in the sky

22:47.830 --> 22:52.630
Forget about the hands of the clock for now

22:52.630 --> 22:57.040
Try taking one deep breath

22:57.040 --> 23:06.670
The rainbow-colored scenery
will resonate with my heart

23:08.000 --> 23:13.000
I'm sure any wish I have will come true

23:13.000 --> 23:17.540
Because you're by my side

23:17.540 --> 23:22.130
You make every day feel like a dream

23:22.380 --> 23:26.920
At that warm and kind place

23:26.920 --> 23:34.080
Keep showing me your smiling face forever

23:46.000 --> 23:47.420
<b>Next Time</b>

23:47.420 --> 23:50.920
<b>Episode 10</b>

23:47.420 --> 23:50.920
<b>Princess Yuri</b>

23:47.420 --> 23:50.920
<b>Next Time</b>
